  "overview": {
    "text": "The Higgs boson is an elementary particle associated with the Higgs field, a quantum field thought to fill space. It can be understood as a ripple, or excitation, of that field. Interactions with the field give mass to certain fundamental particles, including W and Z bosons, electrons, and quarks; the boson itself is not a particle that simply gives everything its mass. The field and the Brout–Englert–Higgs mechanism help explain why the W and Z carriers of the weak force are massive. ATLAS and CMS experiments at CERN’s Large Hadron Collider announced the particle’s discovery in 2012. Its spin is zero, a distinctive property that helped establish its identity.",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://home.cern/science/physics/higgs-boson/",
      "https://www.energy.gov/science/doe-explainsthe-higgs-boson",
      "https://home.cern/science/physics/higgs-boson/ten-years/"
    ]
  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "text": "The Higgs boson is a ripple, or wave, in the Higgs field; finding it provided evidence for the field.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://home.cern/science/physics/higgs-boson/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Brout–Englert–Higgs mechanism describes how interactions with the field give mass to certain fundamental particles, including W and Z bosons.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://home.cern/science/physics/higgs-boson/",
        "https://www.energy.gov/science/doe-explainsthe-higgs-boson"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The photon does not interact with the Higgs field and has no mass.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://home.cern/science/physics/higgs-boson/",
        "https://www.energy.gov/science/doe-explainsthe-higgs-boson"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ATLAS and CMS announced the discovery in 2012; further measurements helped confirm the particle’s spin-zero nature in 2013.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://home.cern/science/physics/higgs-boson/",
        "https://home.cern/science/physics/higgs-boson/ten-years/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Higgs mechanism was proposed in 1964 by Peter Higgs, François Englert, and other theorists.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.energy.gov/science/doe-explainsthe-higgs-boson"
      ]
    }
  ],
